            to be both
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcountable"} subcountable
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countably+indexed"} countably indexed
          %h2#unprovability Unprovability
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              There exists a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boolean+topos"} boolean topos
              in which the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
              holds and the continuum hypothesis fails.
          %p
            One topos for which the theorem holds is called the
            = succeed ";" do
              %em Cohen topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+topology"} dense topology
            (also called the
            = succeed "-topology)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo ¬
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \neg\neg
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↪
                  %msup
                    %mn 2
                    %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N} \hookrightarrow A\hookrightarrow 2^{\mathbb{N}}
            but no monomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \hookrightarrow N
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi N
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^N \hookrightarrow A
          %p
            The Cohen topos will be constructed from the topos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            of sets. For this, recall that the subobject classifier of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Set
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2\coloneqq \{0,1\}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forcing"} forcing
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (Cohen poset)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
              be the set of natural numbers; i.e. the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers+object"} natural numbers object
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              be a set with strictly larger cardinality
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %msup
                          %mn 2
                          %mi ℕ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {|A|}\gt {|2^\mathbb{N}|}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≔
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mn 2
                          %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\coloneqq 2^{2^{\mathbb{N}}}
              will do because of the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+argument"} diagonal argument
              %em Cohen poset
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is defined to be the set of morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi p
                    %mo →
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:F_p\to 2
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi p
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi A
                    %mo ×
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_p\subseteq A\times \mathbb{N}
              is any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
              subset. The order relation on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is defined by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi iff
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi q
                    %mo ⊇
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi p
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi and
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q\le p\; iff\; F_q\supseteq F_p\;and\;q|_{F_p}=p
            %p
              where the right-hand condition means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              restricted to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_p
              must coincide with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %p
            We think of each element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            as an approximation to the function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo →
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:A\times\mathbb{N} \to 2
            that is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential"} transpose
            of the putative monomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mn 2
                    %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:A\to 2^\mathbb{N}
          %p
            with “smaller” elements considered as better approximations. The very rough intuition is that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo →
                  %mi q
                  %mo →
                  %mi …
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\to q\to \dots
            (if
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ≥
                    %mi q
                    %mo ≥
                    %mi …
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\ge q \ge \dots
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codirected+diagram"} codirected diagram
            of monomorphisms with domains of increasing size whose colimit is
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
            (i.e. forming (pre)sheaves) we obtain a topos in which this colimit exists.
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+topology"} dense
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcanonical+topology"} subcanonical
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\in P
              we have
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y(p)=hom(-,p)\in\Sh(P,\neg\neg)
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ×
                        %mi ℕ
                    %mo :
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi P
                              %mo →
                              %mi Set
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi p
                              %mo ↦
                              %mi A
                              %mo ×
                              %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_{A\times\mathbb{N}}:\begin{cases}P\to Set \\ p \mapsto A\times\mathbb{N}\end{cases}
              denote the functor constant on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\times\mathbb{N}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo :
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi P
                              %mo →
                              %mi Set
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi p
                              %mo ↦
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi b
                              %mo ,
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi p
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi b
                              %mo ,
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo =
                              %mn 0
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                              %mo ⊆
                              %mi A
                              %mo ×
                              %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C:\begin{cases}
                    P\to Set
                    \\\
                    p\mapsto \{(b,n)|p(b,n)=0\}\subseteq A\times \mathbb{N}
                    \\end{cases}
            %p
              Then we have
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi C
                    %mo =
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\neg}{\neg} C=C
              in
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Sub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ×
                          %mi ℕ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sub(k_{A\times\mathbb{N}})
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              is a closed subobject with respect to the dense topology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo ¬
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\neg}{\neg}
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+of+subobjects"} algebra of subobjects
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi k
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo ×
                          %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k_{A\times\mathbb{N}}
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Psh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Psh(P)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo ¬
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_{{\neg}{\neg}}
            denote the subobject classifier of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(P,\neg\neg)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ω
                    %mrow
                      %mo ¬
                      %mo ¬
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_{{\neg}{\neg}}
            is given by the equalizer
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mo ¬
                        %mo ¬
                    %mo =
                    %mi eq
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi id
                      %mi Ω
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega_{{\neg}{\neg}}=eq(id_\Omega,{\neg}{\neg})
          %p
            By the preceding lemma, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+morphism"} characteristic morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi χ
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi_a
            of the subobject
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℕ
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi k
                    %mi A
                  %mo ×
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} k
                    %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \colon C\hookrightarrow k_{A\times\mathbb{N}}=k_A\times\k_\mathbb{N}
            factors through some
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ×
                        %mi ℕ
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mo ¬
                        %mo ¬
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon k_{A\times\mathbb{N}}\to \Omega_{\neg\neg}
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_3 Lemma
            %p
              The adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi k
                      %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mrow
                        %mo ¬
                        %mo ¬
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi k
                          %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:k_A\to \Omega_{{\neg}{\neg}}^{k_{\mathbb{N}}}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a monomorphism.
          .num_corollary
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              The associated-sheaf functor sends
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              to a monomorphism in the Cohen topos.
          %h2#unrefutability Unrefutability
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is a model of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZF"} ZF
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
            both hold in Gödel’s
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructible+universe"} constructible universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            built from
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            as well.
          #GCHinZF.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Regarding the statement of the
              %em generalized
              continuum hypothesis in
              %em ZF
              (not ZFC), one should distinguish various possibilities. One might leave the statement
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ℵ
                          %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ℵ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^{\aleph_n} = \aleph_{n+1}
              unchanged, so that the GCH becomes a statement just about ordinals or well-ordered sets. But then one could argue such a generalized continuum hypothesis is not as general or strong as it might be, since not all sets can be well-ordered using ZF alone. The more general statement would say that if there are monomorphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to P(X)
              for infinite sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              is bijective with one of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, P(X)
            %p
              For example, Sierpiński proved that over ZF, the generalized continuum hypothesis implies AC. (See
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hartogs+number"} Hartogs number
            %p
              In weakly predicative mathematics, power sets do not exist, so the stronger version of the continuum hypothesis for Dedekind real numbers would have to be rephrased in terms of the Sierpinski space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕊
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{S}
              and function sets: if there are monomorphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝕊
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to \mathbb{S}^X
              for infinite sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              is bijective with one of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝕊
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, \mathbb{S}^X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to Y
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y \to \mathbb{N}^X
              for infinite sets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              is bijective with one of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %msup
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X, \mathbb{N}^X
          %h2#EastonTheorem Generalization: Easton’s theorem
          %p
            Just how flexible can the power
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operation"} operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi κ
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mn 2
                    %mi κ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa \mapsto 2^\kappa
            be? There are of course some constraints. Obvious ones are that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi κ
                  %mo &lt;
                  %msup
                    %mn 2
                    %mi κ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa \lt 2^\kappa
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mn 2
                    %mi κ
                  %mo ≤
                  %msup
                    %mn 2
                    %mi λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^\kappa \leq 2^\lambda
            whenever
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa \leq \lambda
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%B6nig%27s+theorem"} König's theorem
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi cof
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mi κ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa \lt cof(2^\kappa)
          %p
            where the right side is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofinality"} cofinality
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^\kappa
          %p
            A remarkable illustration of the power of the forcing method is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Easton%27s+theorem"} Easton's theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinals"} regular cardinals
            go, these are really the
            %em only
            constraints.
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a{:href => "#Easton70"}> Easton 70
                )
            %p
              Suppose
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model"} model
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZFC"} ZFC
              in which the generalized continuum hypothesis (GCH) holds. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+function"} partial function
              from the class of infinite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinals"} regular cardinals
              to the class of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinals"} cardinals
              such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  is strictly increasing and preserves the order
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo ≤
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                  is less than the cofinality of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi κ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(\kappa)
                  for all
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi κ
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi dom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa \in dom(F)
            %p
              Then there is a generic extension
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}[G]
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}
              with the same cardinals and cofinalities, such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℳ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ⊧
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mi κ
                    %mo =
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi κ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}[G] \models 2^\kappa = F(\kappa)
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi dom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa \in dom(F)
          %p
            On the other hand, the behavior of the power operation on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+cardinal"} singular cardinals
            is not so unconstrained. For example, in a model of ZFC, the smallest cardinal for which GCH fails can never be singular. The so-called “
            %span.newWikiWord>
              pcf theory
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/pcf+theory"} ?
            ” (or “possible cofinalities theory”), due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saharon+Shelah"} Saharon Shelah
          %h2#links Links
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Stanford Encyclopedia of Philosophy,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://plato.stanford.edu/entries/continuum-hypothesis/"} The Continuum Hypothesis
            %li
              %p
                MO
                %em Solutions to the Continuum Hypothesis
                \. (
                %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/23829/solutions-to-the-continuum-hypothesis"}> link
                )
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Bell"}> J. L. Bell
                ,
                %em Set Theory - Boolean-Valued Models and Independence Proofs
