          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+proof"} formal proof
            of the independence of the continuum hypothesis from
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZFC"} ZFC
          %ul
            %li#Han18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jesse+Han"}> Jesse Han
              ,
              %em Flypitch project – Formal proof of the independence of CH
              (
              %a{:href => "https://github.com/flypitch"}> github:flypitch
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://github.com/flypitch/flypitch-notes/blob/master/forcing-notes.pdf"} pdf
          %p published as
          %ul
            %li#HanvanDoorn20
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jesse+Han"}> Jesse Michael Han
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Floris+van+Doorn"} Floris van Doorn
              = succeed "," do
                %em A Formal Proof of the Independence of the Continuum Hypothesis
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1145/3372885.3373826"} doi:10.1145/3372885.3373826
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2102.02901"} arXiv:2102.02901
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Gratzer"}> Daniel Gratzer
              \:
              %em On The Independence of the Continuum Hypothesis
              (2019) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.danielgratzer.com/papers/on-the-independence.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Gratzer-IndependenceOfCH.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %blockquote
                %p
                  In these notes we present a short, mostly self-contained proof of the independence of the continuum hypothesis. The development is
                  = succeed ":" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos-theoretic
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
                  which can model
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZFC"} ZFC
                  for which the continuum hypothesis fails. […] With these notes I hope to illustrate the elegant
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theoretic
                  approach to
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forcing"} forcing
                  results that has become increasingly common in logic,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
          %p
            For the failure of the continuum to be equivalent to the powerset of the natural numbers in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
          %ul
            %li#Bauer22
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrej+Bauer"}> Andrej Bauer
              ,
              %em The countable reals
              (
              %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4CBFUojXoq4"}> video
              ).
          %p
            That the continuum hypothesis might have been regarded as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+axiom"} fundamental axiom
            in an alternate timeline:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joel+David+Hamkins"}> Joel David Hamkins
              ,
              %em How the continuum hypothesis could have been a fundamental axiom
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.02463"}> arXiv:2407.02463
              \&amp;rbrack;
